    "slug": "mogadishu-youth-lead-climate-action-on-international-youth-day",
    "summary": "On August 12, Somali youth joined global observances of International Youth Day, spotlighting their role in climate resilience and community development in Mogadishu.",
    "content": "On August 12, young people in Mogadishu participated in events marking International Youth Day, an annual global observance established by the United Nations in 1999 through Resolution 54/120. The day serves as a platform to highlight the contributions of youth to economic, political, and technological transformations worldwide.\n\nThis year’s focus centered on climate action, with local youth groups organizing tree-planting drives and workshops on environmental sustainability. Organizers emphasized that Somali youth are not just beneficiaries of international attention but active agents of change in their communities, particularly in addressing the impacts of climate change on agriculture and livelihoods.\n\nThe observance traces its origins to the 1998 World Conference of Ministers Responsible for Youth in Lisbon, which recommended that the UN designate a day to celebrate and promote youth participation. Since then, August 12 has become a moment for governments, civil society, and diaspora groups to reflect on youth policies and investment.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this day underscores the potential of diaspora youth to bridge global networks and local initiatives. Many diaspora-led organizations have supported education and skills programs in Somalia, aligning with the day’s theme of empowering young people to drive sustainable development. In Mogadishu, participants also called for greater government and international support to translate youth energy into long-term economic opportunities.\n\nThe events concluded with a call for policymakers to involve youth in decision-making processes, particularly on climate and employment. As Somalia continues to rebuild, the engagement of its young population is seen as critical to shaping a resilient and prosperous future.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/12/xuska-maalinta-caalamiga-ah-ee-dhallinyarada-adduunka/",
