    "summary": "Sheikh Abdullahi Zulfa, a renowned singer from the Hobollada Iftin troupe, returned to Mogadishu after more than three decades abroad. He was welcomed by Somali ministers, marking a moment of cultural reunion for the diaspora and homeland.",
    "content": "Sheikh Abdullahi Zulfa, a celebrated figure in Somali music and a former member of the Hobollada Iftin troupe under the Ministry of Education, has returned to Mogadishu after an absence of over 30 years. His arrival on Tuesday was met with a warm reception, underscoring his enduring legacy in Somali cultural life.\n\nZulfa was part of a generation of artists who shaped the nation's musical identity in the 1970s and 1980s, a period when the Hobollada Iftin group played a pivotal role in promoting educational and social themes through song. For decades, he lived abroad, keeping the memory of his art alive among Somalis in the diaspora.\n\nThe welcoming ceremony was attended by the Minister of Defense and the Minister of Information, Culture, and Tourism, who hailed his return as a homecoming of cultural significance. Their presence signaled the federal government's recognition of the arts as a bridge between generations and communities.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, Zulfa's return evokes nostalgia and a sense of reconnection with a homeland that has endured decades of change. His music, once a staple of school curricula and public broadcasts, remains a touchstone for many who grew up during that era. The event also highlights the ongoing efforts to preserve and revitalize Somalia's cultural heritage.\n\nAs Zulfa reacquaints himself with a transformed Mogadishu, his presence may inspire renewed interest in the country's rich artistic traditions, offering a message of continuity and hope. His journey underscores the enduring ties between the diaspora and their homeland, reinforcing the cultural bonds that transcend distance and time.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/11/fannaankii-hore-ee-hobollada-iftin-sheekh-cabdullaahi-zulfa-oo-dib-ugu-soo-laabtay-muqdisho-30-sano-ka-dib/",
